  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When the reaction is carried out in solvents of low polarity such as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CHCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CS</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and at low temperature, monobromophenols are formed.&nbsp;</p><p>When phenol is treated with bromine water,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo></math> tribromophenol is formed as white precipitate.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0087_c4dffcc0cf4e.png\" style=\"width: 392px; height: 335px;\" /></p>"
